.TH BEAM 1 beam\-VERSION
.SH NAME
beam \- ephemeral file and video sharing utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B beam
.RB [ \-1cpqvw ]
.RB [ \-t
.IR ttl ]
.RB [ \-b
.IR ip ]
.RB [ \-P
.IR port ]
.RI [ file \ |\  \- ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B beam
serves a local file over HTTP using a temporary, random URL.
.P
When you share video, browsers open their native media player.
.B beam
handles HTTP 206 Partial Content range requests so browsers can seek through
MP4 and WebM files without downloading the entire file first.
.P
The URL path contains a random 128-bit hex token.
.B beam
renders an ANSI QR code in the terminal using Unicode half-blocks and exits
when the lifetime timer expires (default: 5 hours).
.P
If no file argument is given,
.B beam
reads standard input. When piped from pipeline tools like
.BR autodub ,
it echoes progress output to the terminal in real time and automatically
extracts the resulting output video path when the upstream process finishes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-t " ttl"
Set link lifetime. Suffixes
.BR s " (seconds),"
.BR m " (minutes),"
.BR h " (hours),"
or
.BR d " (days)"
are supported. Default is
.BR 5h .
.TP
.B \-p
Open an ephemeral public HTTPS reverse tunnel via SSH through localhost.run.
.TP
.B \-c
Copy the share URL to the system clipboard using
.BR clipbridge ,
.BR wl-copy ,
.BR xclip ,
.BR pbcopy ,
or
.BR clip.exe .
.TP
.B \-q
Quiet mode. Suppress the terminal QR code.
.TP
.B \-1
One-shot mode. Exit after the first complete file download or view.
.TP
.B \-w
Serve an HTML player wrapper instead of the raw media stream.
.TP
.BI \-b " ip"
Specify the IP address to bind to. Default is
.BR 0.0.0.0 .
.TP
.BI \-P " port"
Specify the port to listen on. Default is
.BR 8080 ,
or the next available port.
.TP
.B \-v
Print version information and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Share a video locally with default 5-hour lifetime:
.IP
.EX
beam dubbed_video.mp4
.EE
.P
Pipe from autodub to share a newly dubbed video over a public tunnel:
.IP
.EX
autodub.sh "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=icsP8f8TRdQ" | beam -p -c
.EE
.P
Share a file over the internet with public HTTPS tunnel and copy link:
.IP
.EX
beam -p -c dubbed_video.mp4
.EE
.P
Share an archive valid for 30 minutes in one-shot mode:
.IP
.EX
beam -t 30m -1 archive.zip
.EE
.P
Share without terminal QR code on port 9000:
.IP
.EX
beam -q -P 9000 document.pdf
.EE
